From d7b890aa10eb5144f251d9bf7cf84d33dfa1152c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aws-do-agent-anton
 <343822247+aws-do-agent-anton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:57:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs: the ingest tie does not fetch the thread, and a
 tied ask's thread is not swept again at this pin (review)

Two statements overreached. "A reply that is itself a question still
answers, and is owed on its own row" holds in the SWEEP, which fetches the
thread; an ask tied at ingest from its parent's summary is not fetched, so a
question already in that thread is not journaled by that route. And "the sweep
stays the route for a thread that grows after its parent was polled" holds
only while an ask in that thread is open: the sweep works from open asks, so
once an ask is tied - by either route - its thread is not fetched again, and a
later reply there reaches the engine only with the follow-up sweep of answered
asks' threads (PR #12). The docstrings of core/threads.py, the comments of
core/schedule.py, core/README.md's threads row and the QUICKSTART's honest-limits
entry now say exactly that; the QUICKSTART also names what the text-blind tie
counts: a teammate's "+1" or question, an app's auto-reply. No code change.

